thena spine> data Nat : Type₀ where { zero : Nat ; succ : Nat -> Nat }
declared Nat
thena spine> open Nat
opened Nat
thena spine> :revalidate
valid
thena spine> :goal Nat
▶ let ? goal : Nat in
  goal
thena spine> :revalidate
valid
thena spine> :extract
stuck: not finished: the hole goal is still open, so there is no term yet
thena spine> certify core`Nat`
stuck: not finished: the hole goal is still open, so there is no term yet
thena spine> along
thena core> unify core`goal` core`zero`
solved: goal
thena core> :extract
let goal = zero : Nat in goal
thena core> certify core`Nat`
certified
thena core> certify core`Nat -> Nat`
the kernel refused it
in the term:
  let goal = zero : Nat in goal has type Nat
    but Nat -> Nat was expected
    Nat -> Nat and Nat do not match
thena core> :revalidate
valid
thena core> back
thena spine> assume "A" core`Type₀`
thena spine> :extract
λ (A : Type₀) -> let goal = zero : Nat in goal
thena spine> certify core`Nat`
the kernel refused it
in the term:
  λ (A : Type₀) -> let goal = zero : Nat in goal has type Type₀ -> Nat
    but Nat was expected
    Nat and Type₀ -> Nat do not match
thena spine> :quit
